---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import ShuleHome from "@/assets/images/shuleflow-home.png";

import ShuleChat from "@/assets/images/shuleflow-whatsapp-1.png";

import ShuleFees from "@/assets/images/shuleflow-whatsapp-2.png";

import "@/assets/css/main.css";
---

<Layout>
    <main>
        <div class="wrap top">
            <a class="back" href="/projects">&larr; Back to all projects</a>

            <h1>ShuleYetu — WhatsApp-First School Management</h1>

            <p class="lead">
                A multi-school Django platform that brings school-fee enquiries,
                M-Pesa payments, receipts and announcements into WhatsApp.
                School teams manage students, parents, enrollments, fee
                structures and payment records from a role-aware admin
                dashboard. Parents don't need to install another app.
            </p>

            <dl class="meta">
                <div>
                    <dt>Client</dt>

                    <dd>Own product</dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <dt>What I did</dt>

                    <dd>
                        Product design, Django application architecture, admin
                        workflows, WhatsApp automation, M-Pesa integration,
                        payment and receipt processing, debugging and testing.
                    </dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <dt>Year</dt>

                    <dd>2026</dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <dt>Status</dt>

                    <dd>
                        Core product complete, additional development and
                        piloting in progress
                    </dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="wrap">
            <figure class="shot wide">
                <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

                <div class="slot">
                    <Image
                        src={ShuleHome}
                        alt="ShuleYetu admin dashboard"
                        loading="eager"
                    />
                </div>
            </figure>

            <section>
                <div class="narrow body-copy">
                    <h2>The problem</h2>

                    <p>
                        Fee enquiries, statements, payment confirmations and
                        school announcements can create a steady stream of
                        manual work. Staff need to identify the right student,
                        confirm what has been paid, allocate money correctly and
                        get the information back to the parent without losing
                        track of conversations or receipts.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The same issue also arises with sending payment
                        receipts, annouceents, fee changes, and other important
                        information. Parents also have to reach out to staff if
                        they want to know whats happening in the school.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        In Kenya, WhatsApp is a familiar communication channel
                        and M-Pesa is a familiar way to pay. ShuleYetu connects
                        those everyday tools to a school's underlying student,
                        billing and payment records, reducing the need to move
                        between disconnected manual processes.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>

        <section class="band">
            <div class="wrap">
                <h2>What I built</h2>

                <div class="feats">
                    <div>
                        <h3>A school inside WhatsApp</h3>

                        <p>
                            Parents message their school's WhatsApp number and
                            get a simple menu, using list and reply buttons as
                            well as typed options. They can identify themselves,
                            link their children, check a fee balance, request a
                            fee statement, information or school announcement
                            without leaving the chat.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>M-Pesa fee payments</h3>

                        <p>
                            Paying fees triggers an M-Pesa STK push straight to
                            the parent's phone through Safaricom's Daraja API.
                            Once the payment is confirmed, the parent gets a
                            receipt on WhatsApp and the school sees the payment
                            recorded against the right student.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Parents also have the option of paying via M-pesa
                            paybill with debit and credit card payments coming
                            soon. The management system uses the parent's phone
                            number and student's admission number to align and
                            allocate payments.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Multi-school by design</h3>

                        <p>
                            Many schools run on one system. Each school has its
                            own WhatsApp number, so the number a message arrives
                            on identifies the school. Staff accounts are tied to
                            a school through memberships with roles such as
                            admin, finance and staff, so people only see and
                            edit their own school's data. Only a super admin
                            sees across schools.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Student and parent management</h3>

                        <p>
                            Students, parents, enrollments, grades, terms and
                            academic years are managed in the admin. A parent
                            can be linked to several children, and parents can
                            be selected right from the student form.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Conversations and enquiries</h3>

                        <p>
                            Every conversation and message is recorded. Messages
                            from numbers that aren't registered are stored as
                            prospects for the receiving school, since they are
                            often new parents looking for a place.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>Announcements and support</h3>

                        <p>
                            Schools can send announcements to all parents,
                            specific parents, or parent whose children are in a
                            specific grade on WhatsApp, a channel they already
                            read, and parents can ask questions or request help
                            without phoning the office.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h3>School admin dashboard</h3>

                        <p>
                            Built on Django Unfold, giving school staff a modern
                            admin for fees, payment tracking, parent
                            communication and basic reports without a custom
                            back office.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Grade-based fee structures</h3>
                        <p>
                            Fee structures are associated with a grade and
                            academic period. The admin workflow makes the
                            structure visible alongside grade details and
                            enrolled students, while billing services apply
                            charges to eligible enrollments with
                            duplicate-charge prevention as a key invariant.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Payment records and receipts</h3>
                        <p>
                            The payment workflow connects a confirmed M-Pesa
                            transaction to the relevant student account and
                            allocation, then creates a PDF receipt and tracks
                            receipt notification separately from the payment.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Webhook and transaction handling</h3>
                        <p>
                            WhatsApp events and Daraja callbacks are handled as
                            distinct integration paths. Development has covered
                            cancelled STK requests and failed payment states,
                            while idempotency, reconciliation and recovery from
                            interrupted processing remain part of hardening.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="pair">
                    <figure class="shot half">
                        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                        <div class="slot">
                            <Image
                                src={ShuleChat}
                                alt="ShuleYetu WhatsApp menu"
                                loading="lazy"
                            />
                            <figcaption>WhatsApp parent interaction</figcaption>
                        </div>
                    </figure>

                    <figure class="shot half">
                        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                        <div class="slot">
                            <Image
                                src={ShuleFees}
                                alt="ShuleYetu fees admin"
                                loading="lazy"
                            />

                            <figcaption>School fees flow</figcaption>
                        </div>
                    </figure>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="band">
            <div class="narrow body-copy process">
                <h2>How it's built</h2>

                <h3>Why WhatsApp and M-Pesa first</h3>

                <p>
                    A new app asks parents to install software, remember
                    credentials and learn another interface. WhatsApp provides a
                    familiar entry point, while M-Pesa supports the payment
                    step. ShuleYetu connects these channels to structured school
                    records rather than treating messages and payments as
                    isolated events.
                </p>

                <p>
                    This version of the software is intentionally focused on the
                    operational journey tht includes identify the parent and
                    student, retrieve fee information, initiate payment, process
                    the provider's result, record the payment and issue a
                    receipt. That creates a testable foundation before expanding
                    into a broader school ERP.
                </p>

                <h3>Multi-school architecture</h3>

                <p>
                    ShuleYetu is a Django project organized around school,
                    student, academic, billing, payment, document and WhatsApp
                    responsibilities. A custom email-based user model can be
                    linked to schools through memberships and roles. Admin
                    querysets are scoped to the staff member's school, and
                    school ownership is populated by the application where
                    appropriate. A super administrator can work across school
                    boundaries.
                </p>

                <h3>WhatsApp and payments</h3>

                <p>
                    The bot receives WhatsApp Cloud API webhook events and uses
                    conversation state to track the current step and selected
                    student. It can respond with numbered options, interactive
                    lists and reply buttons. Conversations and individual
                    messages are persisted, and unregistered senders can be
                    retained as prospects instead of disappearing as unmatched
                    inbound traffic.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Fee payments use Safaricom Daraja STK Push to prompt the
                    parent's phone. The callback is the provider's result signal
                    since the application records success or failure and links
                    confirmed payments to the appropriate allocation.
                </p>

                <p>
                    A receipt document and a receipt-notification record are
                    separate concerns, so a WhatsApp delivery problem should not
                    undo a confirmed payment.
                </p>

                <h3>Billing and payment lifecycle</h3>
                <p>
                    The payment path is designed as a sequence of explicit
                    records, with the path including an initiated transaction, a
                    provider callback, a confirmed payment, a student-account
                    allocation, a PDF receipt and a WhatsApp delivery attempt.
                </p>

                <p>
                    This separation makes it possible to investigate where a
                    flow stopped without confusing a successful payment with a
                    failed notification.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The project also includes a shared confirmed-payment service
                    so STK and Paybill/C2B payments can reuse the same
                    allocation and receipt logic.
                </p>

                <h3>Admin workflows that reflect school operations</h3>
                <p>
                    Django Unfold provides the operational interface. Grade
                    pages bring together enrolled students and fee structures.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Student enrollment views show admission numbers in read-only
                    form and fee structures are managed against the relevant
                    grade and term.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Applying a new fee structure is handled through billing
                    services, with duplicate-charge prevention treated as an
                    important invariant.
                </p>

                <ul class="tags">
                    <li>Python</li>

                    <li>Django</li>

                    <li>Django Unfold</li>

                    <li>WhatsApp Cloud API</li>

                    <li>M-Pesa Daraja</li>

                    <li>PostgreSQL / SQLite development</li>
                    <li>PDF receipt generation</li>
                    <li>Webhook processing</li>
                    <li>Structured logging</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="wrap">
                <h2>Where it stands</h2>

                <div class="results">
                    <div class="res">
                        <strong>Piloting stage</strong><span
                            >Core parent journey built and tested against the
                            Daraja sandbox and deployed to one school</span
                        >
                    </div>

                    <div class="res">
                        <strong>Fees → Payments → Communication</strong><span
                            >The order the product is being built and validated
                            in</span
                        >
                    </div>

                    <div class="res">
                        <strong>1 → 5 → 20 → 100+</strong><span
                            >The target path from one pilot school to a network
                            of schools</span
                        >
                    </div>
                </div>

                <blockquote>
                    Parents don't need another app. We bring the school to the
                    parent through WhatsApp, with M-Pesa integrated into the
                    experience.<cite>The idea behind ShuleYetu</cite>
                </blockquote>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="band">
            <div class="wrap next">
                <a class="proj" href="/projects/pos-system"
                    ><small>Next project</small><span class="t"
                        >Retail POS System</span
                    ></a
                >

                <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects">View all work</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
            <div class="wrap cta">
                <h2>
                    Need a similar website, platform or tool for your business?
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Tell me what you're building and I'll reply with next steps.
                </p>

                <a
                    class="btn"
                    href="mailto:kengitahi\@proton.me?subject=Project%20enquiry"
                    >Start a project</a
                >
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
